From d0463f927afb9e245320a088b86603651cda9932 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(deepseek_v4_1): add SM121 TileLang DFly2 block
 speculative decoding

Base: vLLM 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus the spark-ds41f-1126
(candidate-74) series (0001..0869).

Rationale:
1. AngelSlim/DS-V4.1-Flash-DFly2-B6 (DFlyDeepseekV41DraftModel) implements
   Tencent AngelSpec DFly2 (arXiv:2611.34776): a KV-cache-free, 6-token
   non-causal block backbone (3 DeepSeek-V4.1 mHC + shared-MLA + 128-expert
   top-3 MXFP4 MoE layers reading target SWA + compressed-MLA KV and top-512
   DSA indexers at layers 28/32/36) followed by a 5-step sequential
   self-forced hidden + gated-attentive correction head.
2. Add native SM121 TileLang DFly2 kernels (vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/dfly2.py)
   and model execution (vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/dfly2.py):
   - Extend sparse_mla_fwd_v41 with segments_only=True and row_stride_div
     (1 for correction, 6 for block backbone) so both SWA (128 tokens) and
     top-512 compressed-MLA context attention reuse the warp-specialized SM121
     decode kernel while emitting [rows, H, 2, 512] partial numerators and
     [rows, H, 2] log-sum-exp in log2 space.
   - Fuse RoPE block-key dot products, learned sink bias, gated relative bias
     (sigmoid(gate_logits + gate_bias) + rel_bias), and log2 online softmax
     combination into @tilelang.jit backbone and correction merge kernels, plus
     a single-launch dfly2_prepare_step_kernel that extracts anchor positions,
     last_hidden_states, SWA slot tables, and < anchor_pos masked top-k indices.
   - Reuse TileLang mHC pre/post/collapse, BF16/MXFP8 projections, grouped
     inverse-RoPE + WO-A/WO-B, 128-expert MXFP4 MoE, L2 prefetch plans, TP3
     uneven head/group padding (64 -> 72 heads, 8 -> 9 o_groups), and PP>1
     target embedding loading.
3. Add V2 DFly2Speculator (vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dfly2/) with zero
   draft KV cache, zero lookahead slot reservation, separate_draft_input_tokens=6,
   dedicated workspace lane 1, per-batch [1..max_num_seqs]*block_size FULL CUDA
   graph capture, vocabulary-parallel top-2 greedy sampling, and online IRLS
   margin confidence calibration for adaptive verification and sink rejection.

Quality:
Target model outputs remain governed by exact block verification / rejection
sampling; draft model runs in native BF16 dense + MXFP4 routed-expert precision
with bit-exact greedy parity against an independent AngelSpec reference on both
synthetic weights and the full 2,392-tensor DS-V4.1-Flash-DFly2-B6 checkpoint.

Tests:
77/77 CPU gate and DFly2 tests passed on dgx4 (test_dfly2.py: SpeculativeConfig
auto-detection, TP3 uneven head padding, end-to-end numerical parity and
rejected-index masking, full 2,392-tensor DS-V4.1-Flash-DFly2-B6 load + parity,
and SM121a TileLang kernel lowering; plus test_direct_loader.py,
test_deepseek_v4_1_prepare.py, test_deepseek_v41_serving_contract.py, and
test_register_quantization_config.py).

Upstream-status: Local deployment patch pending upstream vLLM DFly2 support.

